Rule 7 (input and target tensors have different shapes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) ≠ shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 8 (input tensor cannot have dimensions of size zero)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 9 (target tensor cannot have dimensions of size zero)
{v_2 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 10 (input and target tensors must have same shape along the first dimension when input has more than 1 dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 then shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 11 (when input is 1D, target should be 1D)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then ndim(v_2) = 1
